/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (31. \(A\) Plot B was treated with chemical fertilizers. They supply nutrients quickly, so crop yield rises suddenly. But long-term use reduces soil fertility and kills useful microbes, leading to a gradual decrease in yield. \(B\) Plot A was treated with manure. Manures release nutrients slowly, improve soil texture, water-holding capacity, and increase soil fertility gradually. Hence, yield increases steadily, though with some delay. \(C\) Reason for different patterns:)
/E (31. \(A\) Plot B was treated with chemical fertilizers. They supply nutrients quickly, so crop yield rises suddenly. But long-term use reduces soil fertility and kills useful microbes, leading to a gradual decrease in yield. \(B\) Plot A was treated with manure. Manures release nutrients slowly, improve soil texture, water-holding capacity, and increase soil fertility gradually. Hence, yield increases steadily, though with some delay. \(C\) Reason for different patterns:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
